And `ConsumeIntegralInRange`:
```cpp
template <typename T>
T ConsumeIntegralInRange(T min, T max) {
  static_assert(std::is_integral<T>::value, "An integral type is required.");
  static_assert(sizeof(T) <= sizeof(uint64_t), "Unsupported integral type.");
  if (min > max)
    abort();
  T range = max - min;
  T result = min;
  if (range > 0) {
    T base = ConsumeIntegral<T>();
    result = min + base % (range + 1);
  }
  return result;
}
```

For `ConsumeRandomLengthString()` with default `max_length = SIZE_MAX`:
- `range = SIZE_MAX - 0 = SIZE_MAX`
- `range > 0` is true
- `base = ConsumeIntegral<size_t>()` consumes 8 bytes
- `result = 0 + base % (SIZE_MAX + 1)`

But `SIZE_MAX + 1` overflows to 0, so `base % 0` is undefined behavior (division by zero).

