But the check is `treepos > tree->numcodes - 2u`, which is `treepos > 286`. So `treepos` can be up to 286 before the check triggers. With `2 * 286 + 1 = 573`, which is within the 576-entry buffer.

So the tree construction itself won't crash. The overflow in `blcount[15]` only corrupts `nextcode[0]`, which doesn't cause a crash.

